{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The nakedness of your father and the nakedness of your mother you shall not uncover.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it is all one prohibition, and the meaning of the verse is: you shall not uncover the nakedness of your mother, for if you do so you uncover the nakedness of your father, since the nakedness of your mother is the nakedness of your father. And likewise in what follows: ״ערות אחי אביך לא תגלה״ — the nakedness of your father's brother you shall not uncover. Now it is known that the warning applies only to females, and therefore it explained ״אל אשתו לא תקרב דודתך היא״ — to his wife you shall not approach, she is your aunt — as if it said: the nakedness of your father's brother you shall not uncover; and what is the nakedness of your father's brother that you shall not uncover? That you shall not approach his wife, for if you do so you uncover the nakedness of your father's brother." "<b>And by way of the</b> Midrash (razal): they are two prohibitions, for so they expounded: ״ערות אביך״ — the nakedness of your father — this is your father's wife; ״ערות אמך״ — the nakedness of your mother — this is his mother who is not his father's wife. And the fact that it went back and said ״ערות אשת אביך״ — the nakedness of your father's wife — is to include after death. ״ערות אחותך בת אביך״ — the nakedness of your sister, the daughter of your father — who is not from your mother, ״או בת אמך״ — or the daughter of your mother — who is not from your father, ״מולדת בית או מולדת חוץ״ — born in the household or born outside — that is, whether she is your sister from marriage or from harlotry, you must treat the bond of sisterhood with honor and not uncover her nakedness. And the fact that it went back and said ״ערות בת אשת אביך מולדת אביך״ — the nakedness of the daughter of your father's wife, born to your father — it is all one with what it mentioned, ״ערות אחותך בת אביך״ — the nakedness of your sister, the daughter of your father, who is not from your mother — except to incur two prohibitions for her, for one who lies with his sister, his father's daughter who is not his mother's daughter, transgresses on account of ״אחותך בת אביך״ and on account of ״ערות בת אשת אביך מולדת אביך״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:28.550878423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}